f that to go around; they couldn\u2019t hope to stop entire fleets by themselves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mages were forced to hide and flee. The unfortunate few who were captured were forced into cruel and twisted experiments. The very same cunning and knowledge the Orokin used to empower humanity was now turned against those who wanted to enlighten humanity to the Truth of things.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the mages leave the operating table they were not themselves, but rather pawns of some other entity, enslaved in their own minds and able to use the Supernal Truths for the Orokin\u2019s lies. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Neural Sentry\u201d </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> was created to bring the \u201chuman-derived\u201d creatures back into the fold, so that they might serve the Orokin once more. Mages were among the first to be successfully captured and \u201cpacified\u201d. This problem was made even worse when the process became automated and was slowly piecing together a system to find and determine those who were on the cusp of Awakening..</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages did what they could to survive, mostly by fleeing into the shadows or other realms. They hoped and sought the powers above them to destroy their enemy and well into the Old War, the Orokin were undone by their own creations.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Orokin fell and all those who were left were stragglers who had to scavenge to get by, the mages breathed a sigh of relief. Maybe it was for the better that the Orokin fell, in the hopes that their successors would be more receptive of the Truth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Chains of the Void</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Why the Orokin turned on the Mages is a mystery. Even more is how they were even to best and defeat several Masters and enthrall lesser mages to their wills. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Pentacle Orders however propose a simple theory, that the Void, the dimension that the Orokin relied so heavily on was infact a realm that held a connection the Abyss. The technologies used by the Orokin to hunt mages used Void energies in their construction and functions. Even the Neural Sentry must use the taint in its workings for it to be so effective. The Void might have corrupted the Orokin, convincing them to embrace the Lie so utterly.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There a however holes with this theory, most notably of all, Tenno, humans that </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>were</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> corrupted by high levels of Void energy are not beacons of Paradox made manifest. And certainly, actually being in the Void doesn\u2019t really affect a mage\u2019s own powers that much. In fact, some say they have become stronger\u2026 Still, officially, the Pentacle maintans the stance the Void is not to be entered.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Seer Ministries do not know the truth of the matter anymore than the Pentacle, but they\u2019re willing to perpetuate the rumor, especially since it means that they could access the Orokin towers while their rivals may not. Yet, there is always a hint of doubt, a fear that something within the shadows would come and claim them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still, as mages are driven to seek truth above all else, the mysteries of the Void and the Orokin continue to tantalize them so. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mages in the Origin System</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages as always will continue to seek out mysteries as is their nature. The challenges of the Origin System have not changed that.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grineer: Problematic, but manageable. Mages do not really care for the Grineer both because they are worldly problem and because the Grineer rarely produce mages of their own. The Grineer however always constantly act like big brutes, forcing anyone they find to serve them, mage or otherwise. Unlike the Orokin before them, the Grineer are nowhere near as good at mage hunting. Still, most mages do not have plans in the event that a Balor Fomorian and its escort ships aim their guns at a mage\u2019s Sanctum. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: As the direct successors to the Orokin, the Corpus hold the highest number of Void based technologies, most especially the \u201cNullifier\u201d portable bubble shield. The Pentacle Orders maintain never to catch Corpus attention for good reason.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested: A serious threat, especially since the speed at which they can infect a body can often kill and convert a mage into a slavering mutant. Still, most mages do not concern themselves with the infestation, though a few cabals exist to try and find a cure - has not worked yet so far.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno: The Tenno are distrusted by the Pentacle mages, mostly because of their known connection as creatures tainted by the Void. Still, one radical theory held by some, especially some members of the Free Council posit that the Tenno are mages themselves, those that Awakened to a Sixth Watchtower. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this, it's cool, though I wouldn't go as far as to say that the Orokin could figure out a system for predicting Awakenings.<br /> <br /> I would also restrict Mages that have beein Neural Sentry'd to only Legacy powers, Rotes, Praxes and Attainments. Their enslavement to the matter of the Fallen World forever cutting off any access to Creative Thaumaturgy or discovering new Truths.<br /> <br /> Effectively saying: Mages who have been hit with a Neural Sentry may never make any Creative Thaumaturgy, increase their Arcana or Gnosis, nor may they use any Yantras unrelated to the Orokin.<br /> <br /> This also has the bonus of having Magic used by Neural Sentry controlled Mages to look as fancy and gold as the ancient towers around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T06:44:50-08:00","id":816837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816834#post816834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like this, it's cool, though I wouldn't go as far as to say that the Orokin could figure out a system for predicting Awakenings.<br /> <br /> I would also restrict Mages that have beein Neural Sentry'd to only Legacy powers, Rotes, Praxes and Attainments. Their enslavement to the matter of the Fallen World forever cutting off any access to Creative Thaumaturgy or discovering new Truths.<br /> <br /> Effectively saying: Mages who have been hit with a Neural Sentry may never make any Creative Thaumaturgy, increase their Arcana or Gnosis, nor may they use any Yantras unrelated to the Orokin.<br /> <br /> This also has the bonus of having Magic used by Neural Sentry controlled Mages to look as fancy and gold as the ancient towers around them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, I'll adjust this then.<br /> <br /> The Orokin were &quot;rumored&quot; to be develping a counter measure that would have predicted when mages would awaken, but this is mostly just a worst case scenario that the Mages fear with so many being taken. I forgot to edit that in.<br /> <br /> As for the Legacy stuff, well, don't know how that is so I'll just paraphrase you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:08:27-08:00","id":816849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816669#post816669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike most of those who posted here I can't claim any real knowledge of War Frame having only old commercials and online images to go by, but I can't help wondering if you aren't giving this too much thought. Why can't the CofD just be continuing like normal? It's not like the different splats actually control the world or stopped two world wars, most would either have been too busy with their own pursuits to really try or part of it. Even when they did try there would be what one member of a splat for several million (perhaps by now tens of millions) of normal people? That would be like trying to stop the flooding ocean with a really big earth mover, no matter how big or powerful the mover the endless water will just flow around and eventually over it. Couldn't you just get by with creating the 'human' setting and then let the splats fill the same places they do in the modern one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Human&quot; is kind of... warped in Warframe. Manus listed some of the problems, but byfar the biggest problem is the Orokin, the fallen Empire that comes a thousand or so years ago from when the current day of the games take place. They are/were a human civilization that through which all of the current fragmented cultures of the Origin system arose from when they fell.<br /> <br /> To put this rather plainly... they have quite alot of the trappings of a precursor race. They had advanced technology that allowed them to access and create pocket dimensions, directly walk into an alternate reality where the laws of physics are different and then create a bubble of real world physics to exist in, had developed specific technologies to cancel out reality warping, and engineered trees that wouldn't be out of place on Warhammer 40k's Catachan since they can withstand Orbital Bombardment and dogs that could shred powered armor equipped full body cyborgs. I honestly wouldn't blame many modern day mages for mistaking the Orokin as Atlanteans given their feats.<br /> <br /> Oh and they seemed to hate people touched by the supernatural based on their opinion of the Tenno since they considered them monster which honestly would be magnified against all the other <i>actual monsters out there. </i><br /> <br /> Simply put... you can't realistically apply our current understandings of humanity to Warframe, nor can the various splats continue existing as they have in the modern day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-26-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:32:18-08:00","id":816907,"title":"","content":"This is also a consequence of the fact, that when you consider that the Orokin were human of all races, they just seem to be so... Alien?<br /> <br /> I mean, if I was playing Exalted, the Orokin* are EXACTLY what I would expect from a decadent First Age, the stalker mentions them as being &quot;cold and breathless&quot;, their towers seem to be so gold and white and beautiful that it's almost... Unreal?<br /> <br /> The Orokin are possibly more alien than most of the actual monsters in CofD.<br /> <br /> I consider the Orokin to be worse than the True Fae for example.<br /> <br /> *I use the Orokin as my primary inspiration for the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:47:40-08:00","id":816910,"title":"","content":"Can't really comment much here, seeing as I'm still digesting all the interesting twists to the supernatural templates <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, you planning on doing the Werewolves next? I'm rather curious at whether or not the Forsaken and Pure division is still a thing, especially when you factor in the Moon's return from the Void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:54:46-08:00","id":816915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816910#post816910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't really comment much here, seeing as I'm still digesting all the interesting twists to the supernatural templates <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That said, you planning on doing the Werewolves next? I'm rather curious at whether or not the Forsaken and Pure division is still a thing, especially when you factor in the Moon's return from the Void.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yes. Well, after the Corpus (which I will be posting with in an hour) since I already posted Mage and Vampire back to back.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is that this entire project actually started out as a result of me thinking about the implications the moon literally being <i>gone from the sky </i>and the sort of effect it would have on Forsaken society. and well, I liked Warframe so... why not. I've hinted towards some of the effects in my mockup character of Tero Mir in that other thread.<br /> <br /> I actually want to create a Gift involving the Orokin Void, but I'm kinda bad at creating things that aren't just &quot;blasts&quot;.... hm, maybe basing them off of the Tenno's Focus powers? You interested in that idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:02:18-08:00","id":816921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816915#post816915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually want to create a Gift involving the Orokin Void, but I'm kinda bad at creating things that aren't just &quot;blasts&quot;.... hm, maybe basing them off of the Tenno's Focus powers? You interested in that idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear, if this ends up with one of us writing a new Arcanum or something...<br /> <br /> By the way, would you use Forces, Death or Spirit to manipulate the Void?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and the Gift idea sounds interesting. <br /> <br /> Five types of Renown=Five Mod Polarities/Tenno Ways perhaps?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:09:55-08:00","id":816926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816921#post816921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I swear, if this ends up with one of us writing a new Arcanum or something...<br /> <br /> By the way, would you use Forces, Death or Spirit to manipulate the Void?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and the Gift idea sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> Five types of Renown=Five Mod Polarities/Tenno Ways perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly what I was thinking. Not sure if it maps perfectly well, but I can try seeing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd actually use Prime and/or Space actually for the Void manipulations myself.<br /> The Void doesn't seem to be death based and there's certainly little that can be said to be &quot;spirits&quot; as far as we can tell. Forces of course a likely choice, too, but eh, I don't think it's quite close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:10:59-08:00","id":816928,"title":"","content":"Well, I got nothing for your potential Gift, but there is an Abyssal <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Qq4rTwv96anwn9rNd7ZkKWDcL0lEnDo4KerP_LYNAI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of the Void</a> that Falco created. It's still a draft, as he says, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:14:49-08:00","id":816932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816928#post816928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I got nothing for your potential Gift, but there is an Abyssal <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Qq4rTwv96anwn9rNd7ZkKWDcL0lEnDo4KerP_LYNAI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of the Void</a> that Falco created. It's still a draft, as he says, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not what I had in mind. But thanks anyways. Maybe it'll provide a seed for when I decide to whip something up later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and to save on posts, here's the next Warframe faction.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Corpus</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cProfit Numbs the Feeling.\u201d ~ Alad V</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Corpus are but a mere fragment of the once great and mighty Orokin Empire, a Merchant Cult built on the principles of salvaged technology and robotics. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Orokin fell, the survivors became fragmented and factitious. One of these factions was a techsavvy group that was desperate to cling onto the technology and old way of life that was now denied to them. They sought to master the remnants of their technology, rediscovering pieces of what they once were. They clung onto the trade quotas and limits set forth by the now Orokin, hoping that strict adherence would bring them wealth. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Generations later, this greed and love of the past would be the Corpus\u2019s strength for it is they that have inherited the most from their dead masters. The veneration of Orokin technology and culture had practically transformed into a religion, where above all else, Profit, capital P, was the most important value to have. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through their control of the Solar Rails, the Corpus control the entire economy of the Origin System, allowing them near uncontested economic access and control over the flow of Artifacts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nothing is above Corpus greed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Robotics Inbound </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Corpus are genetically identical to the Orokin that preceded them, that is to say, they are perfected humans. Corpus (and other similar humanities) are functionally identical to ordinary humans for the purposes of game rules, save that they may live quite long.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Corpus have a habit rarely showing themselves to other races. In most situations, they simply rely on their robotic servants to either conduct business or fight for them; it is only in matters of extreme importance or when their lives are being threatened directly do the Corpus act on their own behalf. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moas and Ospreys are simplistic robots with a high level animal intelligence. They can follow simple and complex commands such as being told to shoot at specific targets, to guard specific objectives, to haul specific equipment, or even all at once in a preset sequence. They are even capable of recognizing individuals.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus robots are able to be contacted remotely via radio and are able to distinguish their master from opposition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus robotics have their own detailed rules in another section.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Corpus and the Supernatural</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Corpus are a highly superstitious bunch despite being the greatest scientific minds in the Origin System.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a result, they are rather wary of the Supernatural\u2026 not that it stops them from trying to milk the unexplained for credits and platinum.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampires: The Corpus have about as much interest in the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Hemophages </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">as their ancestors did. Their energy weapons are very effective at dispatching unprotected vampires quite readily, dealing their normal damage against such foes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Werewolves: Wild beasts of little relevance in the eyes of most Corpus, however, several Directors have noted the unusual and far reaching powers that some werewolves wield over the world around them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages: High value recruitment target. Corpus, unlike their former masters, are willing to spend quite a bit on \u201cpremium\u201d services. Granted, it helps to have them sever ties with their former associates before having them come to work. Should they be recalcitrant, Nullifiers are on standby not only to handle the Tenno. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changelings: The Corpus are aware of the existence of Changelings and have gone so far as to create an entire \u201cIron Guard\u201d of moas specfically for \u201cdealing with them\u201d. However, most are unsure of whether that means that the Corpus seek to wipe the Changelings out\u2026 or extort them for protection money.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prometheans: The Corpus are wary of such creatures, for they know nothing can cause a deal to turn sour faster than violence erupting. At least, unless you are in the arms and security market.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Giest: The Sineaters are a major unknown to the Corpus, though the sineaters very often deal with them. Other than graverobbing and high prices, the Corpus aren\u2019t really a major concern for Giests as a whole.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mummy: There are rumors that part of the reason that parts of Corpus Culture harken back to an ancient and forgotten time from before the Orokin is because the Corpus hoard the bodies of ancient and forgotten creatures from these times.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demon: As the people willing to sell </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>anything</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> to their customers, it isn\u2019t quite unheard of for demons (preferably in disguise) to go out and buy information from a databroker. Just as well, the Corpus are also willing to sell information </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>on those customers</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> for a higher price. There are also rumors of an &quot;identity market&quot;, though whatever that entails is anyones guess.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-26-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:45:49-08:00","id":816952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=816926#post816926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly what I was thinking. Not sure if it maps perfectly well, but I can try seeing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd actually use Prime and/or Space actually for the Void manipulations myself.<br /> The Void doesn't seem to be death based and there's certainly little that can be said to be &quot;spirits&quot; as far as we can tell. Forces of course a likely choice, too, but eh, I don't think it's quite close enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure we can cook up something?<br /> <br /> Prime is about Truth and ultimate Supernal power, so i'd agree for you with Space.<br /> <br /> Forces for manipulating Void energies and Space for manipulating the Void itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604