r likeable among the Grineer.<br /> <br /> Fear exposes weakness you see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:25:14-08:00","id":817167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817096#post817096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now, I will admit that I am not the greatest fan of Beast, but I can imagine that they'd be rather likeable among the Grineer.<br /> <br /> Fear exposes weakness you see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can only imagine the Corpus have dedicated &quot;Horror houses&quot; for them.<br /> Let's be honest, they'd do it, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, how do you imagine civilian life is? As for myself, I always imagined that most people were spacers who lived in spacestations on or near asteroids. It'd be a little more cyberpunk here...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T19:14:26-08:00","id":817324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817167#post817167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can only imagine the Corpus have dedicated &quot;Horror houses&quot; for them.<br /> Let's be honest, they'd do it, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, how do you imagine civilian life is? As for myself, I always imagined that most people were spacers who lived in spacestations on or near asteroids. It'd be a little more cyberpunk here...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on whose name is stamped on the living space.<br /> <br /> It's probably preferable to live under the Corpus than the Grineer, if only because most people end up working for one of their component businesses. Yes, being a Crewman often sucks, but the Corpus is nothing if not pragmatic; I suspect they treat their actual employees fairly well, because a happy employee is a productive employee, a productive employee is more efficient, efficiency helps profit, hence why the Corpus Crewmen get vacation days according to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4u-cNKqnGD8\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a>. If you're one of their sweatshop workers or it becomes profitable to hang you out to dry, well, them's the breaks, but at least you have a fair shot at getting back into the relatively good life if you become something worthwhile to treat well again. It's still mostly a relative thing though, as the other major power option is the Grineer, who are everything wrong with xenophobia turned up to 30 and then multiplied by the ability to clone &quot;purity&quot; so as to never sully their lineage with other genomes, caught in a death spiral they may or may not be aware of. For you, the one benefit is you won't be killed by Tenno or Syndicates intentionally, otherwise you get to be kicked around by mutant cyborgs all damn day to do the various labors they haven't gotten around to decanting their own workers for on pain of death or worse. The one escape from that life is being able to sneak onto refugee camps in Syndicate or Corpus territory, where life is hard and bitter, but at least your new overlords don't actively begrudge the fact they can't kill you yet. Corpus engineers may even like your Grineer-brand skills at repair and refurbishment.<br /> <br /> Preferably, you'd want to live under the aegis of Syndicates, who are generally messed up from the mercenary perspective of Tenno, but messed up in ways recognizable as human. New Loka and Red Veil are probably the worst to live under but again, it's relative. New Loka just doesn't like transhumanists and probably doesn't quibble with fixing genetic diseases to go back to a purer human form (I doubt they actually quibble with longevity after having lived with that culture for so long), and may actually have a way to fix Grinner decay via introduction of healthier DNA from other sources (possibly why they look askance at Steel Meridian, who are fine with being mutant cyborgs, thank you), and Red Veil is an army of anarchists with a gleefully no-holds-barred approach to warfare, but they're at least ethical enough to get Steel Meridian (an organisation dedicated to protecting refugees, when it comes down to it) on their side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T21:03:45-08:00","id":817384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817324#post817324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends on whose name is stamped on the living space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was asking about nonaffiliated, but then again with the system being so relatively small, there's probably not a whole lot of people. I'm thinking that maybe aside from the canon Syndicates, I perhaps create some of our own.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts occured to me when starting work on the Werewolf snip. What do I do about well, wolves? Do I make it so that all werewolves are technically werekubrows? Or maybe I hint that there's plenty of pockets of nongenetically modified animals both on Earth and off of it (In zoos, preserves, colonization modules)? I mean, there's no evidence for or against wolves being extinct I guess, since the limitations of game design prevent them from existing in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T06:03:15-08:00","id":817546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817384#post817384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I was asking about nonaffiliated, but then again with the system being so relatively small, there's probably not a whole lot of people. I'm thinking that maybe aside from the canon Syndicates, I perhaps create some of our own.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts occured to me when starting work on the Werewolf snip. What do I do about well, wolves? Do I make it so that all werewolves are technically werekubrows? Or maybe I hint that there's plenty of pockets of nongenetically modified animals both on Earth and off of it (In zoos, preserves, colonization modules)? I mean, there's no evidence for or against wolves being extinct I guess, since the limitations of game design prevent them from existing in game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> KUBROWS! KUBROWS! KUBROWS! KUBROWS! KUBROWS! KUBROWS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T06:33:06-08:00","id":817555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817384#post817384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thoughts occured to me when starting work on the Werewolf snip. What do I do about well, wolves? Do I make it so that all werewolves are technically werekubrows? Or maybe I hint that there's plenty of pockets of nongenetically modified animals both on Earth and off of it (In zoos, preserves, colonization modules)? I mean, there's no evidence for or against wolves being extinct I guess, since the limitations of game design prevent them from existing in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go by the assumption that wolves are extinct, then it would only make the werewolves more exotic in appearance for that setting.<br /> <br /> That said, as your opening intro fic to Darkframe implied, the werewolves have adapted best to Earth's forests. And they contribute to the difficulties that the Grineer have in colonizing the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:48:35-08:00","id":817708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=817555#post817555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we go by the assumption that wolves are extinct, then it would only make the werewolves more exotic in appearance for that setting.<br /> <br /> That said, as your opening intro fic to Darkframe implied, the werewolves have adapted best to Earth's forests. And they contribute to the difficulties that the Grineer have in colonizing the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, yeah that's what I was thinking. The Firstborn probably adapted to assimilate Essence from canid successors including Kubrows, but haven't well, shifted in appearance yet.<br /> Werewolves would still bear their ancestral forms perhaps because kubrows are really unnatural.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's probably somewhere wolves still exist, if only because they were transplanted there as part of colonization ops. But Earth is nearly devoid of them since they're being out competed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, the opening intro depicts 5 random splats, the only one that's been confirmed to be there was a Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:57:33-08:00","id":818022,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Werewolves</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha were regarded as little more than beasts in the time of the Orokin, who claimed the Moon for their seat of power. At best they were subhumans who were afflicted by illness, at worst, the werewolves pests to be forced out or put into cages. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the Moon and its spirits buried under golden spires and gleaming archetecture and the Gauntlet being kept under control via mass use of spacewarping technologies, the distinction between the Pure and the Forsaken eroded to nothing. How could the ancient vendettas be maintained when Lunes rarely showed themselves, when Auspices could no longer be given, and when the Firstborn were bound to an Earth that was declared offlimits to Father Wolf\u2019s Children?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They were all forced to survive via whatever means they could, to bind and bargain with spirits that had never heard of their Father, their Mother, or even the Firstborn. Centuries of Orokin dominance had broken and destroyed much of the Urathan culture, for few ever lived so long to convey the stories to the younger generation. Many went their whole lives knowing nothing but what the Orokin said of them or even heading into the spirit world that they did not know and for anyone in such a time, said lives could be quite long.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ironically, it was the loss of the Moon that led to the ressurenge for the people. Without masters clad in gold ruling above them, Earth became accessible once more and werewolves came to find themselves some place someplace very different.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Orokin tended to Old Earth like it was a garden, away from the hands of human intervention to despoil it. When they fell, they left behind a world that harkened back to the Predator\u2019s Paradise that was lost so long ago, a world that ran wild and free. With the Luna lost to parts unknown and the Void technologies used to artificially prevent the Gauntlet from forming weakpoints no longer maintained, the Firstborn, free to step into the physical world for the first time in an untold number of years, hunted as a single pack for the first time in since the Death of Urfarah. They took their wayward and unknowing fleshy cousins and showed them much of what they forgot and the werewolves finally found their place to belong.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Since then, the powers across the Origin system have tried to take over the New Pangea, to subdue the forces that lay claim to it. Most especially, the diseased and unclean descendants of the Orokin servant caste, the Grineer. Under the leadership of Councilor Vey Hek, the armies and fleets above the planet sought to claim it for themselves. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The planet might now have genetically engineered creatures populating every corner of it and normal wolves are a dying breed on the world, but to the werewolves, it is still their home. The Tribes of Urfarah rise to defend it, as outnumbered as they may be. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Moon\u2019s Return.</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In recent memory, the most ominous event to happen to the People as of late, is without a doubt the Moon returning from an extended stay in the Void. When it appeared, the People saw the face of one of their progenitors for the first time in an eon, a damaged and warped planetoid that had been marred by the Orokin and damaged further by its stay in the Void.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lunes appeared in the New Pangea, bringing with them a power thought long lost. Though Mother Luna has remained silent and confusing as ever, the power known as the Auspices were bestowed to her children all over the Solar System\u2026 even those that belong to what were once the Pure Tribes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This has created a bit of a schism within the Tribes of Urfarah, about whether or not they should accept this power, about whether or not that the old blood vendettas that lied long dormant should begin again. Even the Firstborn seem torn over this, as ultimately, Pangea was restored, the very reason their conflict started in the first place.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Moon does not speak, only watches.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Werewolves in the Origin Systeml</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Werewolves continue their hunt. Their prey has changed to include the successor races that came from the old humankind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grineer: The Despoilers of New Pangea are not to be tolerated. They have no claim to their restored homeworld. Though many werewolves can shred even the heaviest Bombard with their claws, they are still massively outnumbered. There are rumors though of Werewolves who had lived their whole lives as one of the Diseased, only to become something pure when the First Change was visited upon him. If this has indeed happened, they do not speak of it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: Werewolves rarely care about the Corpus, as they stick largely to the far reaches of the solar system, more than far enough away for most werewolves to care. Though there is hints that the Orokin\u2019s successors might have information\u2026 or even werewolves in their employ or higher ranks, forming in essence, a Ninth Tribe.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested: The Disease is the second greatest threat to New Pangea after the Grineer as far as the werewolves are concern. It violates mind, body, and place, and seeks to consume all life into itself to feed its twisted hunger. The werewolves believe the bio-weapon to actually be the makings of one of their ancient foes, the</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> Idigam</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, for the only thing more horifing than what the disease does to flesh is the terror of its shadow.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno: To the People, the Tenno are the only ones left in the Origin System that know Honor. It was they who slew the Orokin, and it is they that hold back the Grineer. Those are the things most werewolves care about when it comes to them. Though, there\u2019s more than a few packs that have decided to select the deathless slayers as their favored prey, seeking to test themselves for reason that are difficult to define.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:24:30-08:00","id":818407,"title":"","content":"I have tried my way with a &quot;Gift of the Void&quot; but I have absolutely no ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T07:35:02-08:00","id":818413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=818407#post818407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have tried my way with a &quot;Gift of the Void&quot; but I have absolutely no ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Low priority right now, even though the Werewolf entry was posted above.<br /> <br /> Probably gonna get inspiration from other places to get a Void gift.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, most Void based manipulations seem to be &quot;spacial&quot; or &quot;distortion&quot; based when applied to realspace. Such as Void cloaks used in Tenno lisets, creating or accessing pocket dimensions. Perhaps this should be what we draw upon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, I'm looking at making a Tenno splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of Power Stat being Mastery.<br /> Tenno have no &quot;real&quot; mana equivalent save Energy, which is based on Warframe equipped more than anything.<br /> <br /> Warframes would have ranks, which determine their stats and determine what powers are available. Maybe Mastery instead of determining mana pools, determines how powerful abilitites are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm thinking unsuited Tenno get to use powers for free. Specifically a Void Blast that does constant aggravated damage scaled by Mastery...<br /> <br /> However, you're A. Only limited to very basic Void powers, and B. Mortal and can die.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-28-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T19:57:06-08:00","id":818945,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Tenno</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I am the Lotus. I will guide you, but we must hurry. Vor is coming for you. I see the cryosleep has taken your memory. It does not matter. You are Tenno. I will prepare you.</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot; ~The Lotus</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are many monsters that walked alongside humankind over the countless ages, living in the shadows where man is afraid to go. When the Orokin rose to power, they put an end to this, exploring and choosing to exploit the boundless human potential without fear of the dark. When the War broke out, this Dream ended. The Orokin were forced to return to their home system, to fortify their homelands against traitorous machines. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the Orokin Empire\u2019s darkest hour, those in charge turned towards the twisted and unnatural. They looked towards the a ship full of children, the survivors from the only ship ever to return from a Void jump failure, the Zarimon. Each child was touched by the Void, manifesting powers that defied the natural laws of the universe, a perfect weapon to use against creatures that were engineered to have the Void as a weakness. They gave the survivors of the Ten-0 incident weapons and armor to fight and die for the Orokin; they made their own monsters.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And it worked.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sentients were being forced back, the War was not over yet. For a time, long enough for these warriors clad in armor to develop their own subculture, it seemed like the Orokin were about to win. They began talking about how to best dispose of their would-be saviors, how to keep them away. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And yet, in the final chapters of the Old War, the Orokin were still defeated, by their own creation. The Tenno betrayed them, destroyed their creators for reasons of their own devising. Perhaps they came to realize it was not themselves that were the monsters. Perhaps the Orokin did not realize the entity known as the Lotus that came preside over the Tenno.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tenno then faded into the dark like all the other creatures that lurked in the shadow, their exploits and power becoming a thing of Myth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Second Dream </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When awakened from the Cryosleep, it was as though the Origin System itself shook. Each warrior seemingly unkillable and with veterans equipped with the greatest technology the Orokin could devise. It is not unheard of for entire bases to go missing since every soldier on board was slain down to the last man. </span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno do not often operate their Warframes directly, instead remotely controlling their equipment via a method known only as Transference, in effect, using the Warframe as one would use their own bodies. Transference however requires special equipment, but most Tenno do not leave their Orbiters. And should a Warframe be destroyed? The Orbiter is often able to just teleport the defeated Warframe and rebuild it back to the Oribiter.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, there are times when a Tenno may seek to leave the isolation of their own personal pocket dimensions. Should they do, they give up the majority of their protections\u2026 however it is the best way to find companionship\u2026 or to handle matters in a way that the sword alone may not.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most Tenno are of the same apparent age as they were when the Ten-0 Incident occured, largely the result of excessively long lives and being in stasis pods for most of their existence, but due to errors, deliberate choice, and other factors, Tenno can often appear to be significantly older than the norm.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Tenno and the Supernatural</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tenno are the survivors and elite warriors of the Old War. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vampires: The Tenno are wary of the living dead, and are willing to strike against them should they ever become a threat as great as the Grineer or the Corpus. But for now, they are underwatch.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Werewolves: The Tenno view these predators with some very obvious distrust, but they understand that these \u201cpeople\u201d are unlikely to ever achieve the same destructive capacity as the other races in the solar system due to in large part of how small their populations are and their relatively slow growth. They do however realize these creatures play some role in the balance of a world that the Orokin never quite fully masters.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages: Dangerous not because of the power they wield, but the fact they keep asking questions too much. The Tenno\u2019s Orbiter compartments are shielded enough to prevent a Mage from harming a Tenno through his Warframe, but there is still a fear they will know too much.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changelings: Far too small and rare to be of any relevance, but every now and again, the Tenno find themselves in strange thorny wildlands.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prometheans: Dangerous and threatening madness like some sort of plague, but minor in comparison to other creatures due to massively smaller populations.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Giest: The Sineaters often stalk the Tenno, very sensitive to the sheer amount of killing a single person is capable of.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mummy: These ancients find and odd sympathy with the Tenno, for like themselves, the Tenno seem deathless, returning and destroying all that is asked of them by a higher power. In a strange way, the Tenno seeming in a way acting their successors is not unexpected, after all, every civilization harkened back to old Irem, copying things imperfectly from then\u2026 it was only a matter of time before the Deathless themselves were iterated upon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demon: Perhaps the only people other than a select few to know the truth about the Tenno, several demons having lived long enough to have seen the Tenno when they were first created and having insider knowledge. Demons are very interested in using the Tenno as the Orokin did, as weapons to destroy their enemies.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:51:46-08:00","id":819189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=818413#post818413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Low priority right now, even though the Werewolf entry was posted above.<br /> <br /> Probably gonna get inspiration from other places to get a Void gift.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, most Void based manipulations seem to be &quot;spacial&quot; or &quot;distortion&quot; based when applied to realspace. Such as Void cloaks used in Tenno lisets, creating or accessing pocket dimensions. Perhaps this should be what we draw upon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, I'm looking at making a Tenno splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of Power Stat being Mastery.<br /> Tenno have no &quot;real&quot; mana equivalent save Energy, which is based on Warframe equipped more than anything.<br /> <br /> Warframes would have ranks, which determine their stats and determine what powers are available. Maybe Mastery instead of determining mana pools, determines how powerful abilitites are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm thinking unsuited Tenno get to use powers for free. Specifically a Void Blast that does constant aggravated damage scaled by Mastery...<br /> <br /> However, you're A. Only limited to very basic Void powers, and B. Mortal and can die.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Make a docs so I can help more directly if you do please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:16:10-08:00","id":819207,"title":"","content":"Aside from the Tenno, another issue worth looking into is Shields. We go for ablative protection or a penalty to attacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:39:15-08:00","id":819232,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Tenno, how do you plan on translating the different powers of the Warframes, as well as the Focus abilities of the Tenno schools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:48:57-08:00","id":819241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819232#post819232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Tenno, how do you plan on translating the different powers of the Warframes, as well as the Focus abilities of the Tenno schools?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simple.<br /> <br /> Focus Schools will be the Auspice or Path abilities, and represent abilities specific to a Tenno regardless of Warframe. Unlike in the game, this cannot be changed<br /> When a Waframe is equipped it grants the user 4 powers (which I will cover by going as close as possible to ideal of what the power represent, but some things will have factors like Defense to consider).<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, Well of Life is a Debuff that causes Warframe to regain &quot;health&quot; based on &quot;successes&quot; against a marked target, but it doesn't stun them.<br /> Slash Dash is a quick &quot;Strike multiple opponents with a sword&quot; charge.<br /> Fireball is simplistic enough I don't need to explain it.<br /> <br /> And should an ability drain energy over time, such as World on Fire, well, you get the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-29-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:53:14-08:00","id":819245,"title":"","content":"Ahhh. I see.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:05:59-08:00","id":819589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819241#post819241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Simple.<br /> <br /> Focus Schools will be the Auspice or Path abilities, and represent abilities specific to a Tenno regardless of Warframe. Unlike in the game, this cannot be changed<br /> When a Waframe is equipped it grants the user 4 powers (which I will cover by going as close as possible to ideal of what the power represent, but some things will have factors like Defense to consider).<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, Well of Life is a Debuff that causes Warframe to regain &quot;health&quot; based on &quot;successes&quot; against a marked target, but it doesn't stun them.<br /> Slash Dash is a quick &quot;Strike multiple opponents with a sword&quot; charge.<br /> Fireball is simplistic enough I don't need to explain it.<br /> <br /> And should an ability drain energy over time, such as World on Fire, well, you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most targeted powers should probably take Defense into consideration due to enemy movement.<br /> <br /> I hate targeted powers. I suck at applying them...<br /> <br /> ...which is why I play Mag (HAHAHAHA- Independent movement is a LIE! PULL! CRUSH! PULL! PULL! FUCK YOU CORPUS, SHIELD POLARIZE! FUCK YOU BOSS, BULLET ATTRACTOR!)<br /> <br /> They should probably also use a Skill-agnostic dice pool like Mage's Gnosis + Arcanum, due to the fact that one Mag is just as good as another Mag at pulling people from the right edge of the map to the left no matter how much the other has studied physics.<br /> <br /> But yeah, abilities will be a piece of cake to design, really.<br /> <br /> Also: Focus could maybe grant a fifth Ability through some arcane mechanic we haven't worked out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:09:34-08:00","id":819592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819207#post819207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the Tenno, another issue worth looking into is Shields. We go for ablative protection or a penalty to attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I say ablative protection, there is a distinct difference between armor and shields in Warframe, and it also makes Mag's Shield Polarize <i>so much</i> easier to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:36:21-08:00","id":819607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819589#post819589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yeah, abilities will be a piece of cake to design, really.<br /> <br /> Also: Focus could maybe grant a fifth Ability through some arcane mechanic we haven't worked out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The way I thought about it is that Focus worked like Auspice boons in that a character always has one power determined by Focus... and this ability has a single use per &quot;Story&quot;. No other costs and the player always starts with it. This power is always available to the Tenno regardless of Frame and never changes. They after all represent the innate direction and application of your power to a specific philosophy.<br /> <br /> I mean just because it took most of us 1000 hours to get Focus powers doesn't mean it's the same for all Tenno, right? Some are probably waking up right out of Cryosleep without going through the entire quest chain...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819592#post819592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I say ablative protection, there is a distinct difference between armor and shields in Warframe, and it also makes Mag's Shield Polarize <i>so much</i> easier to write.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. You really like your Mag too btw.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think for the most part how I want Warframe to work on a mechanical level is that we've got the 1 to 10 Mastery that's basically Gnosis. No idea what it's used for, but I say it's a contributing factor to most Powers that need dice.<br /> <br /> Then we've got the Warframes, which go from 1 to 5 &quot;Rank&quot; each.<br /> <br /> <br /> At 1, you get a single basic power<br /> <br /> At every level above the base, the Warframe's stats go up in a manner we determine and you unlock a single power or upgrade an existing power.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> Excal might look like.<br /> 1. Slash Dash.<br /> 2. Radial Blind + Health<br /> 3. Radial Javelins + Shields and Energy<br /> 4. Upgrade Slash Dash to cause Bleeding damage + Armor.<br /> 5. Exalted Blade + all Stats up.<br /> <br /> <br /> My main concern of having Mastery + Rank be the only dicepools is that they'd be... small.<br /> Maybe always had mental attributes to them so that players are encouraged to buff their mental and social abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T05:16:36-08:00","id":819771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819607#post819607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The way I thought about it is that Focus worked like Auspice boons in that a character always has one power determined by Focus... and this ability has a single use per &quot;Story&quot;. No other costs and the player always starts with it. This power is always available to the Tenno regardless of Frame and never changes. They after all represent the innate direction and application of your power to a specific philosophy.<br /> <br /> I mean just because it took most of us 1000 hours to get Focus powers doesn't mean it's the same for all Tenno, right? Some are probably waking up right out of Cryosleep without going through the entire quest chain...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Alright. You really like your Mag too btw.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think for the most part how I want Warframe to work on a mechanical level is that we've got the 1 to 10 Mastery that's basically Gnosis. No idea what it's used for, but I say it's a contributing factor to most Powers that need dice.<br /> <br /> Then we've got the Warframes, which go from 1 to 5 &quot;Rank&quot; each.<br /> <br /> <br /> At 1, you get a single basic power<br /> <br /> At every level above the base, the Warframe's stats go up in a manner we determine and you unlock a single power or upgrade an existing power.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> Excal might look like.<br /> 1. Slash Dash.<br /> 2. Radial Blind + Health<br /> 3. Radial Javelins + Shields and Energy<br /> 4. Upgrade Slash Dash to cause Bleeding damage + Armor.<br /> 5. Exalted Blade + all Stats up.<br /> <br /> <br /> My main concern of having Mastery + Rank be the only dicepools is that they'd be... small.<br /> Maybe always had mental attributes to them so that players are encouraged to buff their mental and social abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps they add a Skill to it? For example Excalibur adds Weaponry to his powers, while Mag adds Science?<br /> <br /> But otherwise I love your ideas, especially the one about Focus abilities being used one per story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T06:45:56-08:00","id":819788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=819771#post819771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps they add a Skill to it? For example Excalibur adds Weaponry to his powers, while Mag adds Science?<br /> <br /> But otherwise I love your ideas, especially the one about Focus abilities being used one per story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright,that works..<br /> <br /> A couple will have Weaponry or Brawl, I guess, but that's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T07:46:24-08:00","id":820968,"title":"","content":"Alright, Manus and I have done some major work on the Tenno and I am satisfied enough to provide much of what was done. Unmarked Spoilers below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Orbiter</u></i></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno require extensive facilities to maintain to their equipment, most especially their Warframes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To this end, the Orokin granted the Tenno Orbiters, specialized vessels to act as mobile resupply bases. Outfitted with the best Void Cloaks, Orbiters are something between ships and personal pocket dimensions for their sole occupant. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Orbiters possess among other things, matter assembly plants, genetic foundries, extensive databanks able to digitally store an entire armory\u2019s worth of mods and gear, and telecommunications able to access nearly the Origin System\u2019s main network ~ all of this controlled by artificial intelligences called a Cephalon, a loyal (if sometimes buggy) servitor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Generally speaking an Orbiter tries to stay within hundreds of thousands of miles of its Tenno in the field. Its specialized cloaking device is such that it completely obscures the Orbiter from a number of means of detection including scanners, scrying, and outright magic.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Due to the nature of the Orbiter, many spells or supernatural abilities designed to affect an inhabitant such as the Tenno himself outright fail unless the caster is already inside the Orbiter itself, as the Void Cloak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That is to say, the Orbiter is not invulnerable. Capital ship weapons will destroy it no problem, it\u2019s just finding the thing that\u2019s the problem.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tenno Template </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Mastery</u></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - While all Tenno are touched by the Void, not all Tenno manifest this power in the same way or have full control over it. Tenno divide themselves into ranks of understanding and power based on how much they have experienced and how much they have access to the Void.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Features:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attribute/Skill cap increases after 5.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No Mana Meter. Energy capacity is determined by Warframe. The Tenno itself does not bother keeping track of personal energy since they are all conduits of Void energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Void blast damage. All Tenno may launch a beam of destructive Void energy from their hands, the damage determined by Mastery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Downsides?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno are mortal, with all the problems that follow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u><b>Focus</b> </u></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The Tenno fought the Old War long and hard, long enough to permanently alter the way their own power could be shaped to specialize to different ends. This is called a Focus, a special and personal understanding of power and how to use it so ingrained into the Tenno, it cannot be changed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Tenno awakening from Cryosleep has a single Focus which bestows a single Focus Power. This power is always available to a Tenno and has no energy cost, but they may only use it once per \u201cStory\u201d representing the uniqueness of this gift.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The 5 Tenno Focus Schools are:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Madurai</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> -</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> \u201cEngage The Enemy\u201d</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Phoenix Gaze</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Zenurik</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cDominate The Enemy\u201d</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Void Pulse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Uniaru</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cOutlast The Enemy\u201d </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Basilisk Flare</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vazarin</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cCounter The Enemy\u201d </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Mending Tides</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Naramon</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cKnow The Enemy\u201d </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Spike</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Syndicate</u></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Each Tenno has the choice of joining an organization of like minded individuals, all in the pursuit of their goals and reasons, even though such groups are not completely comprised of Tenno. Still, Syndicates provide Tenno with resources and material in the pursuit of their state goals.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Joining a Syndicate grants the Tenno access to the Syndicate\u2019s special weapons and items. Leaving a Syndicate causes the Tenno to lose access to these items.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Six Syndicates are available to the Tenno:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Steel Meridian </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perrin Sequence </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Arbiters of Hexis </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Loka </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cephalon Suda </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Red Veil </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warframes</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Tenno do not often send themselves out in the field. For the most part, they operate Warframes remotely from their Orbiters, though there are occasions where they wear their suits into battle, granting them far more power, perhaps near limitless power\u2026 at the cost of mortality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should a Warframe be destroyed, the Tenno may recall it back to their Orbiters for repairs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Operation Rules</u></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When a Tenno operates a Warframe, the Warframe\u2019s physical statistics are used in place of the Tenno\u2019s even when it would be a benefit. Each Warframe comes with the 3 basic Attributes: Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina and is despite being an \u201carmor\u201d is treated as fully living creature possessing Wounds and Health levels as a normal person.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warframes may not be equipped with armor, though they all possess a not so insignificant amount of shielding and armor of their own.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warframes also possess Abilities, usually 4 of them. Some have more. All Abilities cost Energy to run, the amount of which could be stored is determined by the Warframe. Also, Warframes all possess a signature skill used to used the Abilities of a given Warframe. All abilities that require dice rolls involve Mastery + Warframe Rank + this Key Skill.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Each Warframe has a Rank, going from 1 to 5. This determines the overall statistics and abilities of a Warframe. As the Warframe\u2019s rank increases, these statistics and abilities either unlock or increase. All Warframes when first unlocked begin at Rank 1 and possess their first ability. In each Warframe\u2019s entry, it tells you what increasing ranks bestows onto you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Warframe Abilities:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sword Alone: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So long as a Warframe is equipped with a melee weapon and is forgoing ranged combat in order to devote more time and attention to melee, the Tenno may apply his full Defense versus firearms attacks, effectively parrying bullets.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mobility: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warframes are able to leap and travel in ways that a normal human could not, seemingly the result of gravity manipulation. Tenno may run upwards, horizontally, or cling to walls. They may also perform multiply the distances they leap by 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Transference</u></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most Tenno operate their Warframes via transference, the process of remotely operating the Warframe via a remote control rig in the Orbiter. This allows the Warframe to be used as if the Warframe was his own body.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, this means that Void Energy does not flow as quickly to the Warframe as it would otherwise.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using Transference causes the Warframe to start with 0 Energy in its reserve, rising by 1 Energy for every hour the Warframe is operated in this manner for the first 24 hours. Past this point, the Warframe needs to be recalled as the connection between Operator and Warframe is hard to maintain and inefficient. After 24 hours, the Warframe gains only 1 Energy per day.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The main advantage to transference is that the Operator\u2019s life is never in danger, and should the Warframe be lost, another may be made to replace it or the old one can be salvaged.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Suitless</u></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno are heavily discouraged by their \u201cMother\u201d to never leave the Orbiters, yet some do, for reasons of their own. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Suitless Tenno is little more than a human with some Void abilities inherent to their nature.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should a Suitless Tenno need to defend himself, he is always free to use a Voidblast attack. A Voidblast is a simple roll of Willpower + Mastery which on a success deals Aggravated damage equal to Mastery +3</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Direct Use</u></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A few Tenno choose to operate the Warframes regularly, but most Tenno who don a Warframe do so out of desperation. Using a Warframe in this manner is hazardous and risky, but the rewards are by far the greatest.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Tenno in a Warframe provides near limitless Void Energy to the Warframe, providing 1 Energy per minute. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Tenno may still use his Voidblast attack whenever he wishes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><u>Excalibur </u></i></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dexterity</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armor</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3/3. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shields</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 9</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed Factor</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 7 (above human)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Energy </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abilities: Key Skill - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weaponry</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ranks:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Radial Blind, +1 Strength, + 1 Dexterity, +1 Stamina,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Radial Javelin, + 1/1 Armor, + 1 Shield, +1 Energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Strength, +1 Dexterity, +1 Stamina, +2 Energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exalted Blade, +1/1 Armor, +1 Shield, +2 Energy</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Slash Dash</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Ability causes Excalibur to dash between enemies while slashing them to pieces.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Ability causes Excalibur to dash forward in a straight line of 8 meters. Excalibur makes a single attack roll versus the enemy with lowest Defense. This attack does damage to all targets in Excalibur\u2019s path. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Radial Blind</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Ability creates a quick flash of light that blinds nearby enemies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 Energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rank + Mastery + Weaponry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results:</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Something malfunctions and Excalibur takes 1 bashing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The flash of light is not bright enough.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Excalibur emits a bright flash of light, imposing the Stunned Tilt on all enemies within 12 meters. This doesn\u2019t work on enemies that do not have eyes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Ability also imposes the Blinded (Both eyes) Tilt for the remainder of the scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Radial Javelin</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Ability creates a radial explosion of javelins that impale nearby enemies. An enemy that can apply Defense against firearms can also apply Defense against Radial Javelin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Energy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rank + Mastery + Weaponry - Defense if applicable</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results:</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: (No idea)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: This Ability is an attack against all enemies within 15 meters that deals (Rank)L damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The attack also imposes the Stunned tilt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exalted Blade</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Ability summons a sword made of pure light.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Energy per turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Indefinite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While this Ability is active the Tenno gains a (Rank)L weapon with a -0 Initiative Modifier. Whenever Excalibur makes an attack against a target , any enemies behind that target in a line of up to 15 feet take (attack successes + Weapon modifier - number of targets) lethal damage in the form of a wave of light.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 02-01-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T04:43:27-08:00","id":828724,"title":"","content":"We should really write some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:28:10-08:00","id":828744,"title":"","content":"I was taking exams for college. I can start again soon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:25:36-08:00","id":831806,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alright, I got a new snippet.<br /> <br /> Sorry for taking so long.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering: should we have a &quot;Signiture Location&quot;? If so, where should it be?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Prometheans</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is perhaps the greatest irony the universe had ever know that the Prometheans were never considered by the Orokin to be threats or abominations. For reasons that modern dwellers of the Origin system cannot seem to fathom, the creatures that were made to be effigies of humankind were never selected for extermination or mass roundup as all the others have. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever a Promethean was encountered, it was often advised to either leave the creatures alone and vacate the area to prevent being influenced by the Disquiet that affects them\u2026 atleast, so long as Firestorms and serious detrimental effects to the environment were not observed. They did not even seem to care for the transformative powers of the Divine Fire, viewing their own technological wonders: cloning, genetic engineering, robotics, and augmentation as superior.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The creatures were simply left to roam the spheres of Orokin influence, unbothered, unplastered. Perhaps the Orokin pitied them and decided to be merciful. Perhaps they saw no point to bothering with an exotic form of life that was mostly a threat to itself more than anything else. Or maybe, some Prometheans hoped: the Orokin were willing to accept the New Dawn. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Orokin empire died, the Prometheans did not even notice their passing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Wanderers</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Prometheans of today are the creatures that lurked in the darkness that have changed the least. They still wander, avoiding laying down roots in hopes of something greater: the only difference is that they are now unbound from a single world and given more than enough space to avoid humans whether they be in some deserted rock.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still, the main downside to being away from \u2026 everything is that the Azoth that burns in a Promethean has less place to bleed off excess energies and disperse to. As a general rule: Wastelands and Firestorms take 4 times less time to on Spaceships or asteroids.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prometheans in the Origin Systeml</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many Prometheans still seek the New Dawn. Yet, the question of humanity is even more muddled now than it ever was ever since Man could live for centuries and be born from a test tube.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grineer: The most likely producers of modern Demiurges today are Grineer scientists who seek to desperately cure their kind\u2019s genetic weakness and frailties. Instead of using metal and cut up corpses, these mad scientists spend inordinate amounts of time trying to \u201cperfect\u201d a single clone by shifting the forming biomass. Seen as heretical by the majority of Grineer. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: The businessmen do not like dealing with the Prometheans. Often, they are dismissive and just send them away from their installations as soon as they could. Perhaps an insight as to how the Orokin viewed them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested: As far as the Prometheans are concerned, these abborations are Pandorans that hunger for everything and will act as accordingly. Strangely, the Technocyte nano-virus that the Infested utilize to convert flesh and metal into more of itself do not affect a functioning Promethean: perhaps due to Azoth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno: The Prometheans rarely meet Tenno. But when they do, it is with awe and curiosity. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:07:54-08:00","id":839233,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Changeling</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To the Lost, the Orokin were a mixed blessing. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They regarded Changelings as second citizens in their empire, but they were among the few people the Lost believe who could prevent the True Fae from abducting more ever again. Just because humankind reached the stars and became near immortal, that did not stop the monsters from abducting them. No, the Fey came along with them, hitching rides and openning new doorways beyond the Homeworld\u2019s gravity well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">During their Empire, new Changelings were seldomly seen, with the numbers growing fewer with each generation as technology improved. It was thought that the golden clad humans would have eventually isolated Arcadia, barring all doors to it forever more.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hope was destroyed. The Sentients rose, the Tenno rose to prominence, the Orokin fell. It was like listening to a story, about how Precursors would be destroyed by their own creations, letting those who remained to struggle out on the mud.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Without the Orokin to keep them away, the Keepers returned to find a System vulnerable and unknowing of their presentations. Entire ships or even moons would be abducted\u2026 and no one would even notice due to all the chaos that happened in the Fall.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Eternal Tales</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most Changelings today were born or have lived through the worst of the Orokin\u2019s Fall, witnessing first hand the Rise of the Grineer and Corpus to practical empires. Compared to then, the constant, almost orderly power struggle seems almost relaxing when its competition was dozens of factions all competing for the ultimate prize.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the advent of longevity treatments, a time difference of fifty years, though still significant, isn\u2019t \u201cmajor\u201d as compared to how it was before. Often returned Changelings find their homes little changed\u2026 especially since it\u2019s so rare for Fetches to be made to ruin them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Changelings in the Origin Systeml</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changelings are forced to face their masters even more.The True Fae don\u2019t even need to make fetches to escape unnoticed. Entire ships could go missing in the Orokin system and no one would bat an eye, thinking some other menace taken them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grineer: There is very little chance of a Changeling emerging from the Grineer. Just as well, there\u2019s little Grineer do involving Changelings, their detection technology only reveals normal citizens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: Almost as bad as the True Fae, as the Changelings believe that the average Corpus would sell out their own crewmen to the Slavers for quick credits. This does have some backing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested: The average Changeling loathes these creatures, veiwing being mutated by them as yet another abuse to their souls\u2026 one they could never return from like last time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno: Those that know of the Betrayal look at Tenno with almost loathing, for they may not have taken if the Orokin still lived.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T22:32:42-08:00","id":839696,"title":"","content":"So....<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Second Dream unveiled the desolate Moon from The Void. But there was once a time when the Orokin ruled over the Solar System from this prestigious satellite, a home full of awe-inspiring architecture. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The time has come to explore both timelines. Your deft spy skills are called upon as you overcome time-bending challenges on new Moon missions.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the more I think about it, the more my descision to say the Orokin were powerful enough to suppress and fight against mages seems spot on.<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, we're having a Time Travel themed mission now. Maybe not presicely, but... damn.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:34:22-08:00","id":840105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=839696#post839696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the more I think about it, the more my descision to say the Orokin were powerful enough to suppress and fight against mages seems spot on.<br /> <br /> I mean seriously, we're having a Time Travel themed mission now. Maybe not presicely, but... damn.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hype?<br /> <br /> Hype! Hype! Hype!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T15:34:58-08:00","id":843161,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In honor of the newest Warframe, I present the mummies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Mummy</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Arisen have seen the Dawn of Civilization and in many ways the Orokin harkened back to their days.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yet at the same time, the Orokin were different. Humans practically lived dozens of times longer than even the most esteemed elder in those days, and the Orokin studied and observed phenomena that previously only were the domain of gods. Traveling the endless darkness to visit distant worlds, this new generation of man, seemingly earning their gold decorations, grew at a frightening pace.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even more alarming were the creatures, the new life the Orokin made, the machine intelligences known as Cephalons and the nigh all powerful Sentients, were entities that were proof of their mastery. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many of the Arisen came to wonder if there was something of the Shan'iatu or even the Judges themselves spoke of their secret to them\u2026 before this new generation held their scaleps against the ancestor\u2019s chests.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But like all Empires, Nameless or Orokin, the wheel of time shifts. The Orokin fell, undone by their own creations. Some wonder if that is the fate of Irem.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Another Cycle</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is a distant epoch, a future that many struggle to even grasp. The sands that the nameless empire was founded upon have been overrun by a synthetic jungle, and the history of the dozen nations that grew on the remains of Shan'iatus\u2019 work are distant memories. The world that the Arisen came to call home is no longer as important anymore, most of the populace having spread out amongst the myriad of worlds within the Origin System.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In this age, it is exceedingly rare to find any Arisen that still inhabits the same body it did in its original life, the remains having rotted or been eroded over hundreds of lifetimes at this point. Most these days, have undergone the ritual to transfer their Essence to new host bodies at least once.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One noticable upside to everyone being long lived is that the Arisen can often go away from their cults for decades or more and still expect to see the same faces\u2026 allbeit older, but less aged than in previous time peroids.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mummu in the Origin Systeml</span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Judges and Fate still order their servants to act. Not bound by planet, they may still be called to serve. Cults still have need of their gods as well, for even technology does not provide enough power.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grineer: These crude men of flesh and metal are of interest to the Arisen, if not for their technology, but for the potential for ever loyal and eternal servants. Still, at least one mad scientist in this\u2026 cult wishes to hold a few Deathless captive for his own purposes. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: The Deathless know of a secret Heresy among the greedy merchant cult, a sect of mummy worshipers who pride themselves on collecting Relics that improve the value of wealth\u2026 all owned of course by their patron deities. These fanatics of course would wish their leaders were more active\u2026 but what\u2019s a year to these people?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infested: Aberrations, monsters. Corruptions of life. The Deathless are immune to the plague, but their bodies when they lie dormant. And even if they die\u2026 well...</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tenno: The Arisen look at the Tenno and often wonder if that these creatures of the Void might have been set aside for a similar to role to the Arisen themselves, kept asleep for an age so that their patron could awaken them in a time of need. There\u2019s surprisingly many points of similarity.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-08-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:57:39-08:00","id":844083,"title":"","content":"I'll just point out that the <i>Sahu</i> of Mummies are made of Sekhem.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Technocyte Virus can Infest it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Arisen bodies do not rot, they are no longer flesh and bone, but pure Sekhem made flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 03-08-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T12:07:31-08:00","id":844086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=844083#post844083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just point out that the <i>Sahu</i> of Mummies are made of Sekhem.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Technocyte Virus can Infest it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah right. I was more talking about the bodies when the mummy is dormant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:43:45-08:00","id":844381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=844086#post844086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah right. I was more talking about the bodies when the mummy is dormant</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Mummy bodies are something like, barely dust when they are dormant... Let me find my book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy: The Curse p. 142.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=844086#post844086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arisen wear a simulation of living flesh. Their bodies<br /> can barely be called animated corpses, as Sekhem replaces<br /> tissue lost to injury (including the inevitable erosion of the<br /> ages) with a simulacrum the Arisen call the sahu. A sahu is<br /> solidified Sekhem, modeled on the Arisen\u2019s original body\u2014<br /> that is, the body that underwent embalming and a few<br /> necromantic rites in lost Irem. At the start of a new Descent,<br /> the mummy\u2019s Sekhem recreates this template perfectly; for all<br /> his power, he appears to be a withered, dead thingdriven by<br /> unnatural vitality. Fortunately, as the Descent progresses, the<br /> mummy\u2019s Sekhem loosens its grasp on his sahu. The mummy\u2019s<br /> soul reflexively reshapes it into an idealized duplicate of his<br /> original, living form. He can then pass for a normal human<br /> until he is forced to call upon his eldritch magic.<br /> <br /> Based as it is on a ritually altered \u201ckhat\u201d (body), the<br /> sahu is an anatomical oddity. Iremite embalmers removed<br /> every internal organ except for the heart, and scraped<br /> the brain out of its skull. The empty body cavities were<br /> filled with perfumed herbs. As a result, the Arisen possess<br /> a distinctive sweet and bitter scent. At high Sekhem, the<br /> mummy\u2019s flesh turns to its true gray-blue tone and withers<br /> due to his body\u2019s ancient exposure to natron salts.<br /> The mummy\u2019s sahu doesn\u2019t rely on these lost organs<br /> (largely because that is how the Arisen knows and recalls<br /> life), but the Rite of Return allows him to simulate their<br /> functions. The mask of life includes its pleasures... and<br /> to a certain extent, its pains. Mummies can eat, drink,<br /> and bleed, just like the living. Digested matter dissolves<br /> upon contact with a mummy\u2019s empty abdomen. The<br /> Deathless can make love (and those who can recall the act<br /> occasionally feel urged to do so again, with the frequency<br /> of the urges dependent on the personality of the soul in<br /> question), but they are universally infertile, and can thus<br /> neither bear nor sire children, mortal or otherwise. While<br /> the Arisen are truly undead\u2014and thus immune to hazards<br /> such as drowning, hypothermia, and disease\u2014some injuries<br /> that logically should not afflict them do.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:54:49-07:00","id":864151,"title":"","content":"Hey Almarck, I got an idea for Tenno.<br /> <br /> You know how we've been talking about the Tenno powerstat overspecializing them, making them extremely good at murdering at the cost of everything else?<br /> <br /> At Mastery 5 a Tenno is safe.<br /> At Mastery 6 a Tenno takes a -1 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 7 a Tenno takes a -1 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 8 a Tenno takes a -2 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 9 a Tenno takes a -2 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 10 a Tenno takes a -3 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:19:42-07:00","id":864302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=864151#post864151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Almarck, I got an idea for Tenno.<br /> <br /> You know how we've been talking about the Tenno powerstat overspecializing them, making them extremely good at murdering at the cost of everything else?<br /> <br /> At Mastery 5 a Tenno is safe.<br /> At Mastery 6 a Tenno takes a -1 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 7 a Tenno takes a -1 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 8 a Tenno takes a -2 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 9 a Tenno takes a -2 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.<br /> At Mastery 10 a Tenno takes a -3 penalty to any actions that do not attempt to solve a problem with violence or aggressiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know. I hated dice penalties like that sort of thing ever since 1e Werewolf had Social penalties on anything not intimidate.<br /> <br /> I think... instead conditions or &quot;bans&quot; would be a better solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:23:08-07:00","id":864404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=864302#post864302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know. I hated dice penalties like that sort of thing ever since 1e Werewolf had Social penalties on anything not intimidate.<br /> <br /> I think... instead conditions or &quot;bans&quot; would be a better solution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the Ban idea, it also enforces the &quot;honor-bound protector&quot; aspect of Tenno.<br /> <br /> I think that's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:27:49-07:00","id":864407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=864404#post864404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like the Ban idea, it also enforces the &amp;quot;honor-bound protector&amp;quot; aspect of Tenno.<br /> <br /> I think that's great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now we need bans...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T03:35:29-07:00","id":864803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=864407#post864407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now we need bans...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wonderful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:03:30-07:00","id":906738,"title":"","content":"So, I took a glance back at this, and since I am the resident &quot;Mage and Mummy guy&quot; in this thread, I've decided to update the Mages in DarkFrame a bit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Mage</span></span> </b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mages think of the Orokin with fear, revulsion, and most of all, regret.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of all the things that hid in the Shadows, the mages favored the Orokin, for they felt like they had a chance to restore Mankind\u2019s rightful place in the universe, for never before had humanity been so powerful: Understanding of other realities and their exploitation for travel and storage, the ability to grant longevity to everyone, and self aware intelligences. The mages campaigned and supported their rise from the shadows, hoping to cement their hopes for the future, to champion a new era.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It was not meant to be.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Orokin saw the mages, they did not see equals and brothers or teachers to send mankind to the next phase; they saw potential threats and resources to be exploited. The mages rose to defend themselves, but fighting the Orokin was difficult. While no doubt the mages had powerful Masters, the Orokin empire was all too large to be destroyed so easily and there were only so many mages of that to go around; they couldn\u2019t hope to stop entire fleets by themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mages were forced to hide and flee. The unfortunate few who were captured were forced into cruel and twisted experiments. The very same cunning and knowledge the Orokin used to empower humanity was now turned against those who wanted to enlighten humanity to the Truth of things.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the mages leave the operating table they were not themselves, but rather pawns of some other entity, enslaved in their own minds and able to use the Supernal Truths for the Orokin\u2019s lies. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The \u201c</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Neural Sentry\u201d </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">was created to bring the \u201chuman-derived\u201d creatures back into the fold, so that they might serve the Orokin once more. Mages were among the first to be successfully captured and \u201cpacified\u201d. There were even rumors that things were getting worse, with rumors circulating about the Orokin devising a method to predict Awakenings before hand.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages did what they could to survive, mostly by fleeing into the shadows or other realms. They hoped and sought the powers above them to destroy their enemy and well into the Old War, the Orokin were undone by their own creations.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Orokin fell and all those who were left were stragglers who had to scavenge to get by, the mages breathed a sigh of relief. Maybe it was for the better that the Orokin fell, in the hopes that their successors would be more receptive of the Truth.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Chains of the Void</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Why the Orokin turned on the Mages is a mystery. Even more is how they were even to best and defeat several Masters and enthrall lesser mages to their wills. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Pentacle Orders however propose a simple theory, that the Void, the dimension that the Orokin relied so heavily on was infact a realm that held a connection the Abyss. The technologies used by the Orokin to hunt mages used Void energies in their construction and functions. Even the Neural Sentry must use the taint in its workings for it to be so effective. The Void might have corrupted the Orokin, convincing them to embrace the Lie so utterly.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There a however holes with this theory, most notably of all, Tenno, humans that </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>were</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> corrupted by high levels of Void energy are not beacons of Paradox made manifest. And certainly, actually being in the Void doesn\u2019t really affect a mage\u2019s own powers that much. In fact, some say they have become stronger\u2026 Still, officially, the Pentacle maintans the stance the Void is not to be entered.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Seer Ministries do not know the truth of the matter anymore than the Pentacle, but they\u2019re willing to perpetuate the rumor, especially since it means that they could access the Orokin towers while their rivals may not. Yet, there is always a hint of doubt, a fear that something within the shadows would come and claim them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Still, as mages are driven to seek truth above all else, the mysteries of the Void and the Orokin continue to tantalize them so. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Mages enslaved by a Neural Sentry may never increase their Arcana or Gnosis, they may only benefit from Creative Thaumaturgy if they include at least one Yantra inspired or created by the Orokin of old. They may use Legacy Attainments, Praxes and normal Arcana Attainments freely, but Rotes must incorporate Orokin symbols to work.<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mages in the Origin System</span></span> </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mages as always will continue to seek out mysteries as is their nature. The challenges of the Origin System have not changed that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Grineer</i>: Problematic, but manageable. Mages do not really care for the Grineer both because they are worldly problem and because the Grineer rarely produce mages of their own. The Grineer however always constantly act like big brutes, forcing anyone they find to serve them, mage or otherwise. Unlike the Orokin before them, the Grineer are nowhere near as good at mage hunting. Still, most mages do not have plans in the event that a Balor Fomorian and its escort ships aim their guns at a mage\u2019s Sanctum. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Corpus</i>: As the direct successors to the Orokin, the Corpus hold the highest number of Void based technologies, most especially the \u201cNullifier\u201d portable bubble shield. The Pentacle Orders maintain never to catch Corpus attention for good reason.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Infested</i>: A serious threat, especially since the speed at which they can infect a body can often kill and convert a mage into a slavering mutant. Still, most mages do not concern themselves with the infestation, though a few cabals exist to try and find a cure - has not worked yet so far.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Tenno</i>: The Tenno are distrusted by the Pentacle mages, mostly because of their known connection as creatures tainted by the Void. Still, one radical theory held by some, especially some members of the Free Council posit that the Tenno are mages themselves, those that Awakened to a Sixth Watchtower.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:40:53-07:00","id":969729,"title":"","content":"So... in many ways, I've been thinking about what we did wrong here.<br /> <br /> Not to say that the premise was bad, but things in the execution are not as desserving of existance as I recall. Some creative liberties, I could accept, such as leaving the Liset for legwork and all...<br /> <br /> But, I think while thematic, giving each Warframe their own stat cards and level progression system did more harm than good and created unneccesary work and balancing.<br /> <br /> Simplifying that is perhaps more imperative should we proceed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Idea:<br /> Warframe Stats are Static, changing only with Mods.<br /> <br /> Levels revised.<br /> 1-5. as before. But:<br /> 1. is Passive ability.<br /> 2. is 1st ability<br /> 3 is 2nd Ability<br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:09:40-07:00","id":969743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=969729#post969729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... in many ways, I've been thinking about what we did wrong here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=969729#post969729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to say that the premise was bad, but things in the execution are not as desserving of existance as I recall. Some creative liberties, I could accept, such as leaving the Liset for legwork and all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Definetely, none of us want to do a lot of complicated systems that can easily be done with other, existing systems anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=969729#post969729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, I think while thematic, giving each Warframe their own stat cards and level progression system did more harm than good and created unneccesary work and balancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with giving each Warframe it's own stat blok and level progression system, is that it is a fucktonne of work and starts getting into combinatorial hell, where there is a bunch of powers and abilities that all have to be balanced against each other, and then you add mods on and they also have to be balanced against those.<br /> <br /> Which is annoying to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=969729#post969729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplifying that is perhaps more imperative should we proceed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could not agree more, perhaps we divide it into three classes of Warframes, such as Light, Medium and Heavy Warframes, they have a bunch of Attributes that differ based on their class and maybe some Merits to represent their function.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=969729#post969729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea:<br /> Warframe Stats are Static, changing only with Mods.<br /> <br /> Levels revised.<br /> 1-5. as before. But:<br /> 1. is Passive ability.<br /> 2. is 1st ability<br /> 3 is 2nd Ability<br /> And so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems reasonable. We'd have to write a bunch of mods, but they would be simple to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:04:55-07:00","id":970087,"title":"","content":"I also imagine that Tenno get to use Down And Dirty Combat in a whole lot of situations.<br /> <br /> For Shield rules, we want the Tenno to be really good at fighting so I imagine that we could do something like &quot;Shields regenerate at a rate of one point per turn. Any turn in which a Tenno is not attacked, the Shields refresh completely. Should Shields reach a value of zero, they do not refresh and instead only regenerate a single point per turn they do not take damage.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:19:37-07:00","id":970153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=970087#post970087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also imagine that Tenno get to use Down And Dirty Combat in a whole lot of situations.<br /> <br /> For Shield rules, we want the Tenno to be really good at fighting so I imagine that we could do something like &quot;Shields regenerate at a rate of one point per turn. Any turn in which a Tenno is not attacked, the Shields refresh completely. Should Shields reach a value of zero, they do not refresh and instead only regenerate a single point per turn they do not take damage.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how big shield values get. I think a regeneration that scales upwards the more turns you aren't hurt would make sense. 1 for the first turn, 2 for the second.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Down and Dirty works just as well..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:21:01-07:00","id":970217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=970153#post970153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on how big shield values get. I think a regeneration that scales upwards the more turns you aren't hurt would make sense. 1 for the first turn, 2 for the second.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Down and Dirty works just as well..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:22:55-07:00","id":972477,"title":"","content":"Update: A Mage is a great boss battle for Tenno. <br /> <br /> <br /> I had my players play through a session of being newly awakened Tenno that awakened when a highly prestigious Corpus Merchant-Mage came to take a look at what she might sell these Tenno pods for. She possessed a bunch of Forces and Matter, and fought by doing bullshit like hardening the air into shields or disabling Tenno shielding with Forces. After a pretty desperate battle where she flew around a lot and sometimes called Corpus reinforcements consisting of Moa and Osprey units that supported basic Crewmen, they managed to take her down.<br /> <br /> I used the original DarkFrame rules with the rules I presented for shields earlier, and since they were newly awakened they only had their passives. It went pretty well, though I did houserule that Mage Armor of Forces granted you a shield like the ones Tenno use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:19:55-07:00","id":972502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=972477#post972477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update: A Mage is a great boss battle for Tenno.<br /> <br /> <br /> I had my players play through a session of being newly awakened Tenno that awakened when a highly prestigious Corpus Merchant-Mage came to take a look at what she might sell these Tenno pods for. She possessed a bunch of Forces and Matter, and fought by doing bullshit like hardening the air into shields or disabling Tenno shielding with Forces. After a pretty desperate battle where she flew around a lot and sometimes called Corpus reinforcements consisting of Moa and Osprey units that supported basic Crewmen, they managed to take her down.<br /> <br /> I used the original DarkFrame rules with the rules I presented for shields earlier, and since they were newly awakened they only had their passives. It went pretty well, though I did houserule that Mage Armor of Forces granted you a shield like the ones Tenno use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. Guessing the players weren't aware of their &quot;Dreaming&quot; for the first part of the game?<br /> <br /> You do have a rather ridiculous ammount of physical stats at the start. Compared to the monsters that is, so it's not surprising you could put up a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:29:25-07:00","id":972513,"title":"","content":"Also, one change I realize now we should have done from the get go: Use a table to read through everything all at once. One big snapshot instead of having... text like we did before. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:28:05-07:00","id":972541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=972502#post972502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn. Guessing the players weren't aware of their &quot;Dreaming&quot; for the first part of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used it as an introduction to Warframe and they loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:50:13-07:00","id":972549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=972513#post972513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one change I realize now we should have done from the get go: Use a table to read through everything all at once. One big snapshot instead of having... text like we did before.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again, I propose my suggestion of Light, Medium and Heavy Warframes to make things more streamlined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:17:09-07:00","id":972805,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=972541#post972541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used it as an introduction to Warframe and they loved it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting introduction. So they were total newbies to the setting? What was the part they liked, the part where they were more or less murderous space ninjas?<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, I propose my suggestion of Light, Medium and Heavy Warframes to make things more streamlined.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Well, not all Warframes have the same priorities on attributes, especially since DE started playing with the idea of having Frames that buck the Trend, but I see your point. <br /> Maybe we have very basic &quot;Templates&quot; for Light, Medium, and Heavy, but we then alter them to suit the Warframe based on variations of their rules, essentially, adding stuff ontop of the base templates. So, to say to speak, Templates are the most basic or &quot;average&quot; for the category that they're in.<br /> <br /> For instance, when it comes to Inaros, it uses the basic Heavy template, but adds whatever shield values it should have had to health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting 