-setting?p=972805#post972805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the part they liked, the part where they were more or less murderous space ninjas?</div> </div> </div> </div>They like how they get to cut down legions of enemies without repercussions and how the aesthetics look.<br /> <br /> Also, they're in love with the parkour system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting?p=972805#post972805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not all Warframes have the same priorities on attributes, especially since DE started playing with the idea of having Frames that buck the Trend, but I see your point.<br /> Maybe we have very basic &quot;Templates&quot; for Light, Medium, and Heavy, but we then alter them to suit the Warframe based on variations of their rules, essentially, adding stuff ontop of the base templates. So, to say to speak, Templates are the most basic or &quot;average&quot; for the category that they're in.<br /> <br /> For instance, when it comes to Inaros, it uses the basic Heavy template, but adds whatever shield values it should have had to health.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems reasonable. Will return and work on designing a basic framework tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"useri